--[[
	============================================================================
	ROBLOX REAL-TIME STENCIL SHADOW ENGINE (v21 - Retained, Long Range, Stencil-Merged)
	============================================================================
	Client-side (LocalScript / StarterPlayerScripts / executor).

	Look for "[StencilShadow v21]" in the output/F9 console when it starts. If
	you do not see that line you are still running an older copy of the file.

	WHY v20 (v19 was laggy and did not reach far):
	 * Map shadows are RETAINED. They are baked once into their tiles and left
	   alone. Steady state costs almost nothing: no GUI property writes and no
	   re-rasterising of hundreds of shadows every frame.
	 * Everything expensive is budgeted per frame (baking, tile rebuilds, rays),
	   throttled (character light tests / receiver search) and the work is
	   shed automatically by an adaptive quality governor if FPS drops.
	 * Far shadows are cheap: distance-based resolution, size-based culling of
	   tiny far casters, off-screen tiles dropped, no per-edge strokes.
	 * Range: casters up to 3000 studs away, shadows thrown up to 900 studs.

	WHAT STAYS FROM v19
	 * Player shadow = the player's real geometry (package/Rthro body, hair,
	   hats, accessories, tools) rendered from the sun into a ViewportFrame and
	   projected exactly onto the surface the light lands on. The nearest
	   characters get this (MaxSilhouetteCharacters). Without a silhouette the
	   fallback is the real oriented box of every part (limb chains merged,
	   heads as ellipsoids) up close and one merged outline further away.
	 * Nothing is drawn behind walls: shadows only land on the first surface
	   the light reaches; occluders cut their own shadow out of everything behind.
	 * Standing in someone else's shadow: parts in shade are darkened and drop
	   out of the player's own silhouette so the shadows merge.

	Override any CONFIG value before running with:
	    getgenv().StencilShadowConfig = { ShadowDarkness = 0.5, TargetFps = 60 }
	Read live statistics with:  getgenv().StencilShadowStats()
	See the exact player silhouette (red, opaque) with DebugSilhouette = true.
	Print statistics every 5 s with Debug = true.
]]

